      "text": "**Superelevation (banking):** The cross-slope applied in curves. Provides centripetal force partially from gravity instead of tire friction. Maximum superelevation: 8-12% depending on climate (ice risk) and context (urban intersections). Transition from normal crown to full superelevation happens over the spiral/transition section."
